  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040443/assets/68f424470a3a8ff98d7f738ce207c240795185e48ee527a434d04282d9023ed7.png)\n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $y=1$ and $y=4,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\nSo, our differential equation must be\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=(y-1)(y-4)^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $a=1,b=4,$ and $ab=4.$",
